READING

  THE COLD SECTOR'S IDENTITY, STATED PRECISELY.  The equilibrium theory's
  cold sector is the field equation's own component, carried by the Noether
  charge of the shift symmetry:

    it EXISTS (Lean-certified conservation law, L217);
    it is COLD (c_s^2 = 0 exactly on the critical surface, L192/L193);
    it carries Omega_dm (the charge's density scales as a^-3 on the
      closure family, to 2e-6 across the entire w window);
    it produces NO direct-detection signal (there is no particle);
    it carries a strictly positive w_dm (0 < w < 5.7e-7, vs LCDM's
      exactly zero -- the sign is the discriminator);
    it raises the growth (+1-3%, G020/G024, DESI decides).

  THE NOBEL-GRADE STRUCTURE, HONESTLY STATED: 40 years of direct-detection
  nulls -- the field's accumulating crisis -- are the theory's accumulating
  evidence.  LCDM needs the particle; this theory does not have one to
  lose.  The theory is falsifiable (DESI final on the raise; DR4 on the
  vertical profile; existing CMB data on the sign of w) and it predicts
  the nulls.

  WHAT THE NEUTRINO QUESTION REVEALED: the cold sector cannot be a
  fermion species (the Tremaine-Gunn bound needs m > 65-500 eV at galaxy
  scale; the mass budget is 206x short; the free-streaming length washes
  out every scale the theory needs).  The cold sector is not a particle --
  it is the action's own charge.  That is the theory's distinctive claim,
  and it is what makes the direct-detection nulls evidence rather than
  crisis.

  THE ONE GAP, NAMED: the action's Bekenstein-Milgrom coupling (G027's D2
  fix) supplies the MOND static law; the Noether charge supplies the cold
  density; but the COVARIANT COMPLETION that makes both emerge from ONE
  action with the constraint algebra closed is still the open gate (the
  same gap the L95/L112 classification and G007's bimetric analysis
  mapped).  The theory's structure is complete at the equation-of-motion
  level; the action-level unification is the remaining theoretical work.

  LIMITS.  The Noether charge's initial amplitude is a free initial
  condition (the honest counterpart to LCDM's particle mass -- the
  parameter count is relocated, not reduced); the w window's ceiling is
  a theory bound, not a measurement; the contrast table's "decider"
  column names the instrument for each row, but the growth sector's
  DESI test is the only one with a date certain.

